Subject: [PATCH 4/5] v2: F32 reduction auto-vectorization (sum + dot product),
 AVX2 8-wide + SSE2 4-wide

lccc previously detected F32 reduction loops and then rejected them
('Unsupported type for AVX2: F32'), while GCC/Clang vectorize them 8-wide.
Adds Vec{Load,Add,Mul,Zero,HorizontalAdd}F32x{8,4} intrinsics + lowering,
registers them in vector_result_width / regalloc non-GPR exclusion / stack
layout lists, and teaches the reduction transform to emit them.

Two additional defects fixed along the way:
- the accumulator phi-entry rewiring only matched F64/I32 zero constants, so
  the F32 vector zero was DCE'd (8-byte scalar zero vs 32-byte vector load);
- the horizontal-add sequences dropped lanes (AVX2 missed s3, SSE2 shuffled a
  stale register), fixed with vmovshdup / a refreshed shufps source.

Validation: F32 sum/dot match GCC bit-exactly in AVX2 and SSE2 modes over
N in {1..257, 1024}; regression 126/126, correctness 50/50, intrinsics 3/3.
